{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>How</b> — What gift shall I give to HaShem, like 'and return to the king of Israel.'" "<b>And the grammatical analysis of תגמולוהי</b> — it is on the Aramaic pattern of עלוהי, meaning עליו [upon him]. And in my opinion: it is two words, even though it lacks an alef, like לפלמוני [for such-a-one], המדבר את [the one speaking with], עדן, ובבל, ובמה."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 116, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:51.629487050Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}